BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Observational Drawing (6 week series) — Sebastopol Center For th
 e Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260916T000000
DTEND:20260917T000000
UID:919844ceced6f866d78c774df236fb27@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Observational Drawing (6 week series)\n\n  \n    \n      \n   
      \n          $325.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nWednesday Evenings
 \, 6:00-9:00pmSeptember 16th\, 23rd\, 30th\, October 7th\, 14th\, and 21st
   $300.00 + $25.00 Materials Fee Age Requirements: 18+ In this six week c
 ourse\, students will learn and practice observational skills and fundamen
 tal drawing techniques that will inform all of their other creative pursui
 ts. This course is for anyone who wants to practice and advance their dra
 wing skills - beginners\, those who haven’t practiced in years\, or any 
 artists who just want to learn new techniques and practice their skills wi
 th consistent feedback and guidance. Learning to draw is truly learning to
  see - a skill that anyone can be taught\, practice\, and hone. Through de
 monstration\, practice\, and reflective discussion\, this class will explo
 re the foundations of classical drawing techniques in a low pressure envir
 onment. Observational drawing gives all artists a foundation of practical
  knowledge and skills that infinitely expands the possibilities of what on
 e can create. If your ideas feel limited by your drawing skills\, if you f
 eel frustrated or stuck in your painting practice\, or if you simply want 
 to start drawing and are looking for a place to start\, this is the class 
 for you.About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Arts wi
 th an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University of San Diego\, t
 hen attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in printmaki
 ng. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and collected\, bu
 t her art practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor
 . She has taught all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primarily t
 eaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. You can vie
 w her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              
 \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/observational-drawing-6-week-
 series
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
