SUMMARY:Poetry Lives! September 22nd\, 2026 — Sebastopol Center For the 
 Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260922T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
UID:7f8250c09d57c941f75dfb8e3441f308@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Poetry Lives! September 22nd\, 2026\n\n  \n    \n      \n     
  from $5.00\n    \n  \n\nEvery Fourth Tuesday: September 22nd6:00-7:00pm: 
 Spoken Word Workshop 7:15-8:30pm: Open Mic Open to All$5/10/15/20 Sliding 
 Scale for Workshop Join us for an evening of spoken word poetry here at th
 e Sebastopol Center for the Arts! Students of all walks of life\, abilitie
 s\, and experience writing poetry\, or spoken word poetry\, are encouraged
  to join. Students will engage in a freewrite\, poetry reading\, discussio
 n\, and structured writing with a voluntary shareout. After the one hour w
 orkshop\, Poetry Lives! will act as an Open Mic night open to all to read 
 their completed\, or previously completed\, poems. Click here to RSVP to 
 just the Open MicPoetry Lives! is a monthly poetry workshop and open mic s
 eries that aims to create a space for anyone and everyone to come\, learn 
 more about poetic craft\, and share their poetry. The event starts with a 
 facilitated hour-long workshop dedicated to learning craft elements\, disc
 overing new poets\, and generating new work. Once the workshop concludes\,
  we will hold a hosted open mic for anyone who wishes to share. It is not 
 mandatory to participate in the workshop to be a part of the open mic or v
 ice versa. This event is all ages\, but that doesn't necessarily mean fami
 ly-friendly\, as poets are known to cover mature and adult topics from tim
 e to time. About the Poet: Jordan Ranft (He/Him) is a writer and therapis
 t from Northern California. He has been nominated for a Pushcart and Best 
 of the Net. His poetry has been published or is forthcoming in Boulevard M
 agazine\, Frontier Poetry\, Poetry Online\, Bear Review\, Iron Horse Liter
 ary Review\, and elsewhere. His first chapbook\, Said the Worms\, was publ
 ished in June 2023 by Wrong Publishing. He is currently working on a secon
 d chapbook and full-length collection. Instagram: @Jordan_Ranft // @Santar
 osapoetryslam\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Workshop:\n                
 \n\n\n\n                      Select Workshop\n                    \n$5.00
 \n$10.00\n$15.00\n$20.00\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
