UID:cb474a69161aa175e7d01d4b818bf060@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Collage on Panel from Start to Finish - September 26th\n\n  \n
     \n      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nS
 aturday\, September 26th\, 2026\; 11 AM - 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials fe
 eAge: 16+ Join French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz for a new com
 prehensive collage workshop designed to guide you through the complete pro
 cess of creating a finished collage on wood panel. Her hands-on process wi
 ll cover every step—from surface preparation and design to varnishing an
 d wiring.  You will learn presentation tips to give your artwork a profes
 sional finish. What you’ll obtain from this workshop:Reliable methods f
 or preparing your panelTechnical information about selected art materialsC
 reative ways to explore abstraction through collageTechniques for presenti
 ng your artIMPORTANT: Each participant must purchase and bring the followi
 ng items:One 12”x12 cradled wood panel\, gallery style 1 ½” thickOne 
 roll of blue painter’s tape 2” wideOne small Phillips screw driver (cr
 oss-shaped)IMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials ar
 e provided in the attached PDF.  Each participant must purchase and brin
 g the items listed in the attached PDF.Materials provided by Instructor: a
  wide assortment of painted and printed collage papersbrushesacrylic mediu
 mgessovarnishwiring suppliesscissorsThe class will begin with a demonstrat
 ion\, so please plan to arrive early to allow time to settle in.A short lu
 nch break will be held from 12:30 to 1:00 PM. Kindly bring your own lunch 
 and beverage.About the instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American art
 ist whose work is informed by textures and patterns created by the passing
  of time and the effects of the natural elements on the built environment.
   She holds a Bachelor of Science in interior design and she worked in th
 e field of architectural design and green building certification for over 
 25 years.  She has taught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay Ar
 ea and in France since 2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol
  Center for the Arts.  Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she partic
 ipates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyouart
 studio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine’s other classes here:  https://
 wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n   
