UID:1e8c53a3b44ee7256ec5e0b8a04654b5@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Holiday Handbuilding\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          
 $135.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nHoliday Handbuilding Thursdays\, No
 vember 5th\, 12th\, and 19th from 6:00-9:00pm $90.00 Attendance Price + $4
 5.00 Clay Fee = $135.00Maximum of 10 students. Class Description: Get read
 y to deck your halls with handmade charm! Join us for our Holiday Handbuil
 ding Class\, where you will create some holiday themed pieces for the seas
 on of giving using and refining techniques you’ve already tried. In this
  festive workshop\, you will craft your own seasonal treasures\, from cust
 omer ornaments and cozy mugs to unique holiday decor and heartfelt gifts -
  with your hands!  Michael will guide you through numerous demonstrations 
 to help you bring your creative visions to life. Grab a friend\, embrace t
 he holiday spirit\, and build pieces that will become part of your holiday
  tradition!About the Instructor: Michael Citrino has had a love affair wit
 h clay for over 50 years. After his college experience at California Colle
 ge of Arts and Crafts with Viola Frey and further work at Humboldt State U
 niversity with Lew Merrick\, he ran a stained glass business for 18 years.
  Michael and his wife left for Turkey in 1991 to teach in International Sc
 hools. For 26 years he taught K-12 art\, including Ceramics\, Drawing\, Ph
 otography\, Design and Sculpture at schools in six different countries. He
  started clay programs for High School and Middle School students at three
  of those schools. At four of these schools he offered after school and we
 ekend ceramics sessions for teachers and parents. Michael’s work ranges 
 from the traditional to the experimental and a wide swath in between. His 
 approach to teaching is to help students explore the playful nature of the
  clay room and nurture a love for the possibilities that medium presents.\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n         
